comments.body:
@doc77 
I have already enabled xDrip to access my phone's location. 

As for the Bluetooth connection that makes sense. I think I'm remembering back when I had to do something along those lines with the g5 (I might be mistaken though). Regardless it's good to know!

@doc77 
I see what you meant about the phone location now and it has been on. When it comes to the watch settings I don't see why that's important. I do use a polar m600 watch, but the CGM is not sending any data directly to my watch. 

Edit: regardless my watch should have that setting on anyways because I use it for tracking my runs.
